      "created_at": "2012-05-12T16:17:23.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;lugaru&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"lugaru\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>“Flip… an angry Jabberwocky!”</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not to nitpick (I’m totaly nitpicking :P)  but the poem is called Jabberwocky.  The monster itself is the Jabberwock.  /end nitpicky, self righteous correction of the only poem I have memorized in my long term memory because I love all things Alice.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Matchstickman&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Matchstickman\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Really? I never thought of The Matriarch as a haughty woman, more an angsty teenager who never grew up. If she had stamped her foot and exploded into birds that would have been closer to what I imagine The Matriarch as. (Which is not to say I am right)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Theron = grown up Matriarch.  Sure she started out a petulant angsty teenager, but then she grew up and became a badass with control over birds.  Who knows, maybe her powers even evolve to the point that she CAN do some sort of bird turning into thing.</p>",
